# Chat walkthrough for the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
# Start the API (`pnpm dev:api`), index a document or two with documents.http, then send these from
# top to bottom. No secret lives here: export the same variables as for documents.http.
#   SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   KB_EMAIL   KB_PASSWORD

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@supabaseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:54321
@publishableKey = {{$processEnv SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}}
@email = {{$processEnv KB_EMAIL}}
@password = {{$processEnv KB_PASSWORD}}
@token = {{signIn.response.body.$.access_token}}
@conversationId = {{createConversation.response.body.$.id}}
@documentId = {{listDocuments.response.body.$.items[0].id}}

### 1. Sign in; later requests reuse the access token
# @name signIn
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password
apikey: {{publishableKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. Create a conversation → 201; the title stays null until the first message names it
# @name createConversation
POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 3. Ask, streamed → text/event-stream: meta, sources, delta…, usage, done
POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "What changed in the latest release?" }

### 4. A follow-up: rewritten into a standalone query before retrieval (the API logs it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "And what about uploads?" }

### 5. Without `Accept: text/event-stream` → the whole ChatResult as JSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "Summarise the release notes in one sentence." }

### 6. The caller's documents, to pick a scope for the next request
# @name listDocuments
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents?status=ready&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Search only the chosen documents (`documentIds`, at most 20)
POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "What does this document say about limits?", "documentIds": ["{{documentId}}"] }

### 8. The conversation with every message and its citation snapshot (`cited` per source)
GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Conversations, most recently active first
GET {{baseUrl}}/conversations?limit=20&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Rename
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Release notes Q&A" }

### 11. An empty message → 422 invalid_payload with a field error
POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "   " }

### 12. An unknown (or another user's) conversation → 404 not_found, before any stream starts
POST {{baseUrl}}/conversations/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "Hello?" }

### 13. Delete → 204; its messages go with it
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# More than RATE_LIMIT_CHAT_PER_MINUTE (20) messages a minute answer 429 with Retry-After.
